          # Content
          - ::
            type: "section-container"
            name: "Content"
            css: "flex: 1; margin-left: 280px;"
            children::
              - ::
                type: "section-container"
                name: "Top Bar"
                css: "background: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; padding: 20px 40px;"
                children::
                  - ::
                    type: "heading"
                    content: "Introduction to Project Sthalam"
                    css: "color: #111827; font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0;"

              - ::
                type: "section-container"
                name: "Article"
                css: "max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 60px 40px;"
                children::
                  - ::
                    type: "section-container"
                    name: "Status Badge"
                    css: "background: #fef3c7; border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 30px; border-radius: 8px;"
                    children::
                      - ::
                        type: "text"
                        content: "⚠️ POC Status: Sthalam is currently a proof-of-concept. This documentation describes both implemented core functionality and planned features."
                        css: "color: #92400e; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;"

                  - ::
                    type: "markdown-text"
                    mode: "markdown"
                    content: "## What is Sthalam?\n\n**Sthalam** (Malayalam: സ്ഥലം, meaning \"place\") is a sovereign publishing platform that enables individuals to create and distribute content on their own terms—without platforms, algorithms, or intermediaries.\n\nWith Sthalam, you get complete control over your content and how it's distributed. You create websites, micro-blog posts, and newsletters, then share them directly with your viewers through your sovereign node—no middlemen, no terms of service changes, no deplatforming risk.\n\n**Your Data, Your Control**: Everything you create—the blogs you host, the surveys submitted by viewers, the comments on your posts—exists only between you and your viewers. Nobody else has access to it.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Sovereignty\nYou own your content, your identity, and your distribution. No platform can deplatform you, censor your content, or change the rules.\n\n### Direct Distribution\nContent flows directly from your sovereign node to your viewers. No intermediaries, no algorithms deciding who sees your content.\n\n### Cryptographic Ownership\nYour content is protected by cryptographic keys and UCAN tokens. You have provable ownership and control.\n\n### Privacy by Design\nViewers connect directly to your node. Their data isn't harvested by platforms or sold to advertisers.\n\n## What Can You Build?\n\n### Websites\nBuild interactive multi-page websites with visual builders, custom styling, forms, and comment threads.\n\n### Micro-blogs\nPublish Twitter-like posts with real-time collaborative discussions, distributed directly to subscribers.\n\n### Newsletters\nSend rich content directly to subscribers without relying on email platforms or their restrictions.\n\n### Surveys & Forms\nCollect feedback, conduct polls, and gather data from your viewers with complete privacy—only you have access to the results."
                    css: "background: white; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 50px; line-height: 1.8; color: #374151; font-size: 16px;"

