          # Content
          - ::
            type: "section-container"
            name: "Content"
            css: "flex: 1; margin-left: 280px;"
            children::
              - ::
                type: "section-container"
                name: "Top Bar"
                css: "background: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; padding: 20px 40px;"
                children::
                  - ::
                    type: "heading"
                    content: "Comment Threads"
                    css: "color: #111827; font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0;"

              - ::
                type: "section-container"
                name: "Article"
                css: "max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 60px 40px;"
                children::
                  - ::
                    type: "markdown-text"
                    mode: "markdown"
                    content: "## Overview\n\nComment threads in Sthalam enable real-time conversations between publishers and viewers, as well as between viewers themselves. A single document can have **multiple independent comment threads** in different locations.\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Local-First Architecture\n- Comments written to local Yjs doc first (instant UI update)\n- State vector sync for efficient updates\n- Bidirectional synchronization\n- Never transfers full documents\n\n### Permission Model: `crud/write`\n- ✅ Can read existing comments\n- ✅ Can write new comments\n- ✅ Bidirectional flow with all participants\n- ✅ Multi-viewer support\n\n## Try It Out\n\nBelow is a live comment thread. Post a comment to see how real-time collaboration works!"
                    css: "background: white; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 50px; line-height: 1.8; color: #374151; font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 40px;"

