                css: "color: #ffffff; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 30px; padding-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);"
              - ::
                type: "nav-button"
                content: "← Home"
                targetContainerId: "home"
                css: "background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); color: white; padding: 10px 15px; margin-top: 30px; border: none; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 14px; width: 100%;"

          # Content
          - ::
            type: "section-container"
            name: "Content"
            css: "flex: 1; margin-left: 280px;"
            children::
              - ::
                type: "section-container"
                name: "Top Bar"
                css: "background: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; padding: 20px 40px;"
                children::
                  - ::
                    type: "heading"
                    content: "What Makes This Possible"
                    css: "color: #111827; font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0;"

              - ::
                type: "section-container"
                name: "Article"
                css: "max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 60px 40px;"
                children::
                  - ::
                    type: "markdown-text"
                    mode: "markdown"
                    content: "## Core Technologies\n\nOsvauld is built on a foundation of modern peer-to-peer technologies:\n\n### Self-Sovereign Identity\nCryptographic keys (PGP, Ed25519, UCAN) prove your identity without centralized authorities.\n\n### UCAN Authorization\nToken-based permissions for sharing content with specific capabilities.\n\n### CRDT Synchronization\nConflict-free replicated data types enable real-time collaboration.\n\n### Local-First Architecture\nContent renders from local copies with background sync.\n\n### End-to-End Encryption\nAES-256-GCM encryption at rest and in transit.\n\n## The Stack\n\n- **Rust** - High-performance networking\n- **Yjs** - CRDT implementation\n- **libp2p** - P2P networking\n- **PGP** - Asymmetric encryption\n- **AES-256-GCM** - Content encryption\n- **UCAN** - Decentralized authorization"
                    css: "background: white; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 50px; line-height: 1.8; color: #374151; font-size: 16px;"

